# Software Requirements Specification (SRS)

# ScreenQuest – Screen Time Challenge App

## Version

1.0

---

# 1. Introduction

## 1.1 Purpose

The purpose of ScreenQuest is to provide users with a simple web application that helps them monitor their daily screen time, set goals, complete challenges, and build healthier digital habits. This project is developed as a frontend application using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

## 1.2 Scope

ScreenQuest allows users to:

* Track daily screen time manually.
* Set a daily screen time goal.
* View progress through a progress bar.
* Complete daily challenges.
* Maintain daily streaks.
* Unlock achievement badges.
* Use the application on desktop and mobile browsers.

This project does not require user authentication, a backend server, or a database.

## 1.3 Intended Audience

* Students
* Teachers
* Developers
* Anyone interested in improving digital well-being

---

# 2. Overall Description

## 2.1 Product Perspective

ScreenQuest is a standalone frontend web application that runs in a web browser. It stores data locally using the browser's Local Storage.

## 2.2 Product Functions

* Display dashboard
* Set daily screen time goal
* Enter daily screen time
* Show progress percentage
* Display challenge cards
* Track streaks
* Display achievements
* Store user data locally

## 2.3 User Characteristics

Users should have basic knowledge of using a web browser. No technical expertise is required.

## 2.4 Operating Environment

* Windows
* macOS
* Linux
* Android
* Any modern web browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari)

## 2.5 Constraints

* Frontend only
* No backend server
* No online database
* Manual screen time entry

---

# 3. Functional Requirements

## FR1 – Dashboard

The system shall display the user's dashboard with all important information.

## FR2 – Screen Time Input

The system shall allow users to manually enter today's screen time.

## FR3 – Daily Goal

The system shall allow users to set a daily screen time goal.

## FR4 – Progress Tracking

The system shall calculate and display the user's progress using a progress bar.

## FR5 – Daily Challenges

The system shall display predefined daily challenges.

## FR6 – Streak Counter

The system shall track consecutive days when the user meets their goal.

## FR7 – Achievement Badges

The system shall award badges based on completed challenges and streaks.

## FR8 – Local Storage

The system shall save user data in the browser using Local Storage.

---

# 4. Non-Functional Requirements

## Performance

* Fast page loading
* Smooth user interactions

## Reliability

* Data should remain available after refreshing the page.

## Usability

* Simple interface
* Easy navigation
* Responsive design

## Security

* No personal information is collected.
* Data is stored only on the user's browser.

## Compatibility

The application should work on all modern browsers.

